ual is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" · max(|λ|, s\/1000), s Gershgorin’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bound on the spectrum; the vectors are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, whose values are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned. The dense solver below 64 vertices, or when k is a third of them or more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10) for the basis.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"smallest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", every weight is finite","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and nonnegative, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", when given, is at least 1.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"Throws","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"text":" when a Lanczos run spends ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":" products without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"converging, with the products spent and the largest Ritz residual on the tolerance’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scale. The dense solve